<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}" dir="{{ settings.text_direction | default: 'ltr' }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.color_ink | default: '#0D0A06' }}">
  {%- comment -%}
    The four legal pages render the store's own policy text, which Shopify also
    publishes at /policies/…. Two URLs, one document — so each page points its
    canonical at Shopify's copy rather than competing with it. Every other
    template keeps the canonical Shopify worked out for it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign canonical = canonical_url
    if request.page_type == 'page'
      case page.handle
        when 'privacy-policy'
          assign policy_canonical = shop.privacy_policy.url
        when 'return-policy'
          assign policy_canonical = shop.refund_policy.url
        when 'shipping-policy'
          assign policy_canonical = shop.shipping_policy.url
        when 'terms-of-service'
          assign policy_canonical = shop.terms_of_service.url
      endcase
      # shop.<policy>.url is a path, not a URL, and a canonical that reads
      # "/policies/privacy-policy" is resolved against whatever host served
      # the page — including the myshopify domain. shop.url is the primary
      # domain, which is the one the canonical is for. Left alone if Shopify
      # ever hands back something already absolute.
      if policy_canonical != blank
        if policy_canonical contains '://'
          assign canonical = policy_canonical
        else
          assign canonical = shop.url | append: policy_canonical
        endif
      endif
    endif
  -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical }}">

  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%} Default favicon: the logo icon (FS monogram) cropped square {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ 'favicon.png' | asset_url }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ 'favicon.png' | asset_url }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Every collection and hub page carries its own SEO title and description, set
    on the resource itself (scripts/set-seo-meta.py). Two of the signed-off pages
    are built-in routes rather than resources, so there is nothing in the admin to
    attach them to and their copy has to live here:
      /                — the home page, whose SEO otherwise lives in Preferences
      /collections/all — the built-in all-products route
      /collections     — the list-collections hub
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign seo_title = page_title
    assign seo_description = page_description

    if request.page_type == 'index'
      assign seo_title = 'Buy Perfume Online UAE | The Fragrance Secrets'
      assign seo_description = 'Shop authentic designer, Arabic and luxury perfumes for men and women at The Fragrance Secrets. Delivery across the UAE with international shipping to the USA and Canada.'
    elsif request.path == '/collections/all'
      assign seo_title = 'Shop All Perfumes Online UAE | The Fragrance Secrets'
      assign seo_description = 'Shop all perfumes online at The Fragrance Secrets. Browse the complete range of designer and Arabian fragrances for men and women in one place. Fast delivery across the UAE, USA and Canada.'
    elsif request.path == '/collections'
      assign seo_title = 'Shop Perfume Categories UAE | The Fragrance Secrets'
      assign seo_description = 'Browse every perfume category at The Fragrance Secrets. Shop by gender, fragrance type like EDP, attar and oil, and curated lifestyle, climate and brand edits. Fast delivery across the UAE, USA and Canada.'
    endif
  -%}

  <title>
    {{ seo_title }}{% if current_tags %} &ndash; tagged "{{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif -%}
    {%- unless seo_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
  </title>

  {%- if seo_description != blank -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ seo_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Open Graph / Twitter cards. The Igloo theme got these from the Avada SEO
    app, which is not carried over to this theme, so they are emitted here
    from the same seo_title / seo_description the <title> above uses.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'meta-social', seo_title: seo_title, seo_description: seo_description -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Keep filtered / sorted collection URLs out of the index (they are thin duplicates
    of the base collection). The canonical above already points at the clean URL.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if collection -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign is_refined = false
      if collection.sort_by != blank
        assign is_refined = true
      endif
      for filter in collection.filters
        if filter.active_values.size > 0 or filter.min_value.value != blank or filter.max_value.value != blank
          assign is_refined = true
        endif
      endfor
    -%}
    {%- if is_refined -%}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {% render 'fonts' %}
  {% render 'critical-css' %}

  {%- comment -%}
    theme.css and pages.css load asynchronously. Blocking, they cost 790ms
    each before the browser could paint anything, which gated FCP and, behind
    it, LCP — the one metric still failing on mobile. The rules the first
    screen needs are inlined above instead, so the paint no longer waits on a
    network round trip at all; these two arrive in their own time and style
    everything below the fold.

    rel="preload" rather than the media="print" trick: preload asks for the
    file at a sensible priority and the onload flips it into a real
    stylesheet, where media="print" fetches it as a print sheet and can land
    it at the bottom of the queue behind the hero image.

    The noscript copy is not a nicety — without JavaScript the onload never
    fires and the preload never becomes a stylesheet, so the page would be
    left with critical CSS and nothing else.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" as="style" href="{{ 'theme.css' | asset_url }}" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
  <link rel="preload" as="style" href="{{ 'pages.css' | asset_url }}" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
  <noscript>
    {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'pages.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  </noscript>

  {%- comment -%}
    Design tokens from theme settings, injected into :root. Last on purpose:
    theme.css declares the same custom properties at the same specificity, so
    whichever comes later in the document wins. This block used to sit above
    the stylesheet link, which meant theme.css overrode it and the colour
    settings in the theme editor did nothing at all. The four settings happen
    to hold the same values as the CSS defaults, so nothing changes colour
    today — but the setting works now.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    :root {
      --gold: {{ settings.color_gold | default: '#C9A84C' }};
      --cream: {{ settings.color_cream | default: '#F7F2EA' }};
      --ink: {{ settings.color_ink | default: '#0D0A06' }};
      --charcoal: {{ settings.color_charcoal | default: '#1C1812' }};
    }
  </style>

  {%- comment -%}
    Before anything paints, because the class it sets decides whether a
    discount-code box is on the page. Deferred, the box would paint and then
    vanish on every page of a partner-referred session.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'cashback-attribution' %}

  <script>
    /* Base URL for the flat Shopify assets/ folder, consumed by IMG() in app.js */
    window.ASSET_BASE = {{ 'logo.webp' | asset_url | split: 'logo.webp' | first | json }};
    window.CURRENCY = {{ cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency | json }};
    /* Shopify's money filter runs server-side; JS that rebuilds a price after a
       cart change needs the same format string. Consumed by formatMoney(). */
    window.MONEY_FORMAT = {{ shop.money_with_currency_format | json }};
    window.WHATSAPP_NUMBER = {{ settings.whatsapp_number | json }};
    /* collections.js writes its own trust strips and delivery FAQ, so the
       free-delivery figure has to reach JS too — otherwise half the site
       quotes the setting and the collection pages quote a number frozen
       into a script. */
    window.FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD = {{ settings.free_shipping_threshold | default: 250 | times: 1 | json }};
    window.RETURNS_WINDOW_DAYS = {{ settings.returns_window_days | default: 2 | times: 1 | json }};
    window.routes = {
      root_url: {{ routes.root_url | json }},
      cart_url: {{ routes.cart_url | json }},
      cart_add_url: {{ routes.cart_add_url | json }},
      cart_change_url: {{ routes.cart_change_url | json }},
      search_url: {{ routes.search_url | json }},
      predictive_search_url: {{ routes.predictive_search_url | json }},
      all_products_url: {{ routes.all_products_collection_url | json }}
    };
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}
    Microsoft Clarity (project qypu7kamyp) — session recordings and heatmaps.

    This lived in the old Igloo theme's layout and was not carried across in the
    port, so recording stopped the day this theme was published (10 Sep 2026)
    and every recording in the dashboard predates it. Shopify's Customer-events
    custom pixels are sandboxed away from the DOM, so Clarity cannot be moved
    there — a replay needs to read the page. It has to sit in the layout (or
    come from the Clarity app), which means it travels with the theme: carry it
    over if the theme is ever replaced again.

    Loads async and last in the head, so it never blocks first paint.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="text/javascript">
    (function (c, l, a, r, i, t, y) {
      c[a] = c[a] || function () { (c[a].q = c[a].q || []).push(arguments) };
      t = l.createElement(r); t.async = 1; t.src = "https://www.clarity.ms/tag/" + i;
      y = l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0]; y.parentNode.insertBefore(t, y);
    })(window, document, "clarity", "script", "qypu7kamyp");
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}
    GA4 / GTM. Ahead of content_for_header so the container is already open
    when Shopify's own analytics land, and so the dataLayer carries this
    page's context before the first event is pushed.

    Gated on an ID being set, here rather than inside the snippet: with
    neither filled in the layout also skips analytics.js at the end of the
    body, and the context block is only ever read by that file. Rendering it
    anyway would put a kilobyte of inline script in the head of every page
    for no reader — on a theme preview, a staging copy, or a store that has
    not been given its measurement ID yet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.ga4_measurement_id != blank or settings.gtm_container_id != blank -%}
    {% render 'analytics-init' %}
  {%- endif -%}

  {{ content_for_header }}
</head>

<body class="template-{{ request.page_type | handle }}" data-no-chrome data-nav="{{ settings.header_theme | default: 'dark' }}">

  {% sections 'header-group' %}

  <main id="MainContent" class="content-for-layout" role="main" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {%- comment -%} Membership band, above the footer on every page. Whether it carries the welcome discount is decided in snippets/member-band.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}
  {% section 'customer-login-cta' %}
  {% sections 'footer-group' %}
  {% sections 'overlay-group' %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Rendered statically rather than inside overlay-group so its section id is
    literally "cart-drawer". app.js re-renders it through the Section Rendering
    API (?section_id=cart-drawer) after every cart change, and sections inside a
    group get a generated composite id that cannot be requested that way.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% section 'cart-drawer' %}

  {{ 'app.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}
  {{ 'collections.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}
  {{ 'wishlist.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}
  {%- comment -%}
    Last, and deliberately so. analytics.js decorates window.openCart to count
    a mini-cart view, and reads the cart:updated events the three files above
    dispatch — it has to run after they have defined and bound them. It is
    also the one script on the page that nothing else depends on, so it is the
    right thing to have arrive late.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.ga4_measurement_id != blank or settings.gtm_container_id != blank -%}
    {{ 'analytics.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}
  {%- endif -%}
</body>
</html>
